	'messages:apihelp-main-summary' => 'en:',
	'messages:apihelp-main-param-maxlag' => 'en:Maximum lag can be used when MediaWiki is installed on a database replicated cluster. To save actions causing any more site replication lag, this parameter can make the client wait until the replication lag is less than the specified value. In case of excessive lag, error code <samp>maxlag</samp> is returned with a message like <samp>Waiting for $host: $lag seconds lagged</samp>.<br />See [[mw:Special:MyLanguage/Manual:Maxlag_parameter|Manual: Maxlag parameter]] for more information.',
	'messages:apihelp-main-param-origin' => 'en:When accessing the API using a cross-domain AJAX request (CORS), set this to the originating domain. This must be included in any pre-flight request, and therefore must be part of the request URI (not the POST body).

For authenticated requests, this must match one of the origins in the <code>Origin</code> header exactly, so it has to be set to something like <kbd>https://en.wikipedia.org</kbd> or <kbd>https://meta.wikimedia.org</kbd>. If this parameter does not match the <code>Origin</code> header, a 403 response will be returned. If this parameter matches the <code>Origin</code> header and the origin is allowed, the <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> and <code>Access-Control-Allow-Credentials</code> headers will be set.

For non-authenticated requests, specify the value <kbd>*</kbd>. This will cause the <code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> header to be set, but <code>Access-Control-Allow-Credentials</code> will be <code>false</code> and all user-specific data will be restricted.',
	'messages:apihelp-main-param-crossorigin' => 'en:When accessing the API using a cross-domain AJAX request (CORS) and using a session provider that is safe against cross-site request forgery (CSRF) attacks (such as OAuth), use this instead of <code>origin=*</code> to make the request authenticated (i.e., not logged out). This must be included in any pre-flight request, and therefore must be part of the request URI (not the POST body).

Note that most session providers, including standard cookie-based sessions, do not support authenticated CORS and cannot be used with this parameter.',
	'messages:apihelp-main-param-uselang' => 'en:Language to use for message translations. <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+siteinfo|action=query&meta=siteinfo&siprop=languages]]</kbd> returns a list of language codes. You can specify <kbd>user</kbd> to use the current user\'s language preference or <kbd>content</kbd> to use this wiki\'s content language.',
	'messages:apihelp-main-paramvalue-errorformat-html' => 'en:HTML',
	'messages:apihelp-main-param-errorlang' => 'en:Language to use for warnings and errors. <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+siteinfo|action=query&meta=siteinfo&siprop=languages]]</kbd> returns a list of language codes. Specify <kbd>content</kbd> to use this wiki\'s content language or <kbd>uselang</kbd> to use the same value as the <var>uselang</var> parameter.',
	'messages:apihelp-acquiretempusername-summary' => 'en:Acquire a temporary user username and stash it in the current session, if temp account creation is enabled and the current user is logged out. If a name has already been stashed, returns the same name.',
	'messages:apihelp-acquiretempusername-extended-description' => 'en:If the user later performs an action that results in temp account creation, the stashed username will be used for their account. It may also be used in previews. However, the account is not created yet, and the name is not visible to other users.',
	'messages:apihelp-block-param-id' => 'en:The block ID to modify.',
	'messages:apihelp-block-param-newblock' => 'en:Add another block even if the user is already blocked.',
	'messages:apihelp-clientlogin-summary' => 'en:Log in to the wiki using the interactive flow.',
	'messages:apihelp-clientlogin-example-login2' => 'en:Continue logging in after a <samp>UI</samp> response for two-factor auth, supplying an <var>OATHToken</var> of <kbd>987654</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-compare-param-tocontentmodel' => 'en:Specify <kbd>toslots=main</kbd> and use <var>tocontentmodel-main</var> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-compare-param-prop' => 'en:Which pieces of information to get.',
	'messages:apihelp-compare-paramvalue-prop-timestamp' => 'en:The timestamp of the \'from\' and \'to\' revisions.',
	'messages:apihelp-compare-param-difftype' => 'en:Return the comparison formatted as inline HTML.',
	'messages:apihelp-createaccount-param-preservestate' => 'en:If <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+authmanagerinfo|action=query&meta=authmanagerinfo]]</kbd> returned true for <samp>hasprimarypreservedstate</samp>, requests marked as <samp>primary-required</samp> should be omitted. If it returned a non-empty value for <samp>preservedusername</samp>, that username must be used for the <var>username</var> parameter.',
	'messages:apihelp-createaccount-example-create' => 'en:Start the process of creating the user <kbd>Example</kbd> with the password <kbd>ExamplePassword</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-cspreport-summary' => 'en:Used by browsers to report violations of the Content Security Policy. This module should never be used, except when used automatically by a CSP compliant web browser.',
	'messages:apihelp-cspreport-param-reportonly' => 'en:Mark as being a report from a monitoring policy, not an enforced policy',
	'messages:apihelp-cspreport-param-source' => 'en:What generated the CSP header that triggered this report',
	'messages:apihelp-edit-param-baserevid' => 'en:ID of the base revision, used to detect edit conflicts. May be obtained through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+revisions|action=query&prop=revisions]]. Self-conflicts cause the edit to fail unless basetimestamp is set.',
	'messages:apihelp-edit-param-basetimestamp' => 'en:Timestamp of the base revision, used to detect edit conflicts. May be obtained through [[Special:ApiHelp/query+revisions|action=query&prop=revisions&rvprop=timestamp]]. Self-conflicts are ignored.',
	'messages:apihelp-edit-param-returnto' => 'en:Page title. If saving the edit created a temporary account, the API may respond with an URL that the client should visit to complete logging in. If this parameter is provided, the URL will redirect to the given page, instead of the page that was edited.',
	'messages:apihelp-edit-param-returntoquery' => 'en:URL query parameters (with leading <kbd>?</kbd>). If saving the edit created a temporary account, the API may respond with an URL that the client should visit to complete logging in. If this parameter is provided, the URL will redirect to a page with the given query parameters.',
	'messages:apihelp-edit-param-returntoanchor' => 'en:URL fragment (with leading <kbd>#</kbd>). If saving the edit created a temporary account, the API may respond with an URL that the client should visit to complete logging in. If this parameter is provided, the URL will redirect to a page with the given fragment.',
	'messages:apihelp-emailuser-example-email' => 'en:Send an email to the user <kbd>WikiSysop</kbd> with the text <kbd>Content</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-param-revid' => 'en:Revision ID, for <code><nowiki>{{REVISIONID}}</nowiki></code> and similar variables.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-param-prop' => 'en:Which pieces of information to get.

Note that if no values are selected, the result will contain the wikitext, but the output will be in a deprecated format.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-categories' => 'en:Any categories present in the input that are not represented in the wikitext output.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-properties' => 'en:Page properties defined by expanded magic words in the wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-volatile' => 'en:Whether the output is volatile and should not be reused elsewhere within the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-ttl' => 'en:The maximum time after which caches of the result should be invalidated.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-modules' => 'en:Any ResourceLoader modules that parser functions have requested be added to the output. Either <kbd>jsconfigvars</kbd> or <kbd>encodedjsconfigvars</kbd> must be requested jointly with <kbd>modules</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-jsconfigvars' => 'en:Gives the JavaScript configuration variables specific to the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-encodedjsconfigvars' => 'en:Gives the JavaScript configuration variables specific to the page as a JSON string.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-paramvalue-prop-parsetree' => 'en:The XML parse tree of the input.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-param-includecomments' => 'en:Whether to include HTML comments in the output.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-param-generatexml' => 'en:Generate XML parse tree (replaced by $1prop=parsetree).',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-param-showstrategykeys' => 'en:Whether to include internal merge strategy information in jsconfigvars.',
	'messages:apihelp-expandtemplates-example-simple' => 'en:Expand the wikitext <kbd><nowiki>{{Project:Sandbox}}</nowiki></kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-feedcontributions-param-user' => 'en:What users to get the contributions for.',
	'messages:apihelp-feedrecentchanges-param-hidecategorization' => 'en:Hide category membership changes.',
	'messages:apihelp-feedrecentchanges-param-inverttags' => 'en:All edits except ones tagged with the selected ones.',
	'messages:apihelp-feedwatchlist-param-hours' => 'en:List pages modified within this many hours from now.',
	'messages:apihelp-imagerotate-param-tags' => 'en:Tags to apply to the entry in the upload log.',
	'messages:apihelp-import-summary' => 'en:Import a page from another wiki, or from an XML file.',
	'messages:apihelp-import-extended-description' => 'en:Note that the HTTP POST must be done as a file upload (i.e. using multipart/form-data) when sending a file for the <var>xml</var> parameter.',
	'messages:apihelp-import-param-interwikiprefix' => 'en:For uploaded imports: interwiki prefix to apply to unknown usernames (and known users if <var>$1assignknownusers</var> is set).',
	'messages:apihelp-import-param-assignknownusers' => 'en:Assign edits to local users where the named user exists locally.',
	'messages:apihelp-import-example-import' => 'en:Import [[meta:Help:ParserFunctions]] to namespace 100 with full history.',
	'messages:apihelp-linkaccount-summary' => 'en:Link an account from a third-party provider to the current user.',
	'messages:apihelp-linkaccount-example-link' => 'en:Start the process of linking to an account from <kbd>Example</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-login-summary' => 'en:Log in and get authentication cookies.',
	'messages:apihelp-login-extended-description' => 'en:This action should only be used in combination with [[Special:BotPasswords]]; use for main-account login is deprecated and may fail without warning. To safely log in to the main account, use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-login-extended-description-nobotpasswords' => 'en:This action is deprecated and may fail without warning. To safely log in, use <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/clientlogin|action=clientlogin]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-summary' => 'en:Perform management tasks relating to change tags.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-param-operation' => 'en:Which operation to perform:',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-paramvalue-operation-create' => 'en:Create a new change tag for manual use.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-paramvalue-operation-delete' => 'en:Remove a change tag from the database, including removing the tag from all revisions, recent change entries and log entries on which it is used.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-paramvalue-operation-activate' => 'en:Activate a change tag, allowing users to apply it manually.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-paramvalue-operation-deactivate' => 'en:Deactivate a change tag, preventing users from applying it manually.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-param-tag' => 'en:Tag to create, delete, activate or deactivate. For tag creation, the tag must not exist. For tag deletion, the tag must exist. For tag activation, the tag must exist and not be in use by an extension. For tag deactivation, the tag must be currently active and manually defined.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-param-reason' => 'en:An optional reason for creating, deleting, activating or deactivating the tag.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-param-ignorewarnings' => 'en:Whether to ignore any warnings that are issued during the operation.',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-example-create' => 'en:Create a tag named <kbd>spam</kbd> with the reason <kbd>For use in edit patrolling</kbd>',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-example-delete' => 'en:Delete the <kbd>vandlaism</kbd> tag with the reason <kbd>Misspelt</kbd>',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-example-activate' => 'en:Activate a tag named <kbd>spam</kbd> with the reason <kbd>For use in edit patrolling</kbd>',
	'messages:apihelp-managetags-example-deactivate' => 'en:Deactivate a tag named <kbd>spam</kbd> with the reason <kbd>No longer required</kbd>',
	'messages:apihelp-mergehistory-param-from' => 'en:Title of the page from which history will be merged. Cannot be used together with <var>$1fromid</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-mergehistory-param-fromid' => 'en:Page ID of the page from which history will be merged. Cannot be used together with <var>$1from</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-mergehistory-param-timestamp' => 'en:Timestamp up to which revisions will be moved from the source page\'s history to the destination page\'s history. If omitted, the entire page history of the source page will be merged into the destination page.',
	'messages:apihelp-mergehistory-example-merge-timestamp' => 'en:Merge the page revisions of <kbd>Oldpage</kbd> dating up to <kbd>2015-12-31T04:37:41Z</kbd> into <kbd>Newpage</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-opensearch-param-redirects' => 'en:How to handle redirects:',
	'messages:apihelp-opensearch-paramvalue-redirects-return' => 'en:Return the redirect itself.',
	'messages:apihelp-opensearch-paramvalue-redirects-resolve' => 'en:Return the target page. May return fewer than $1limit results.',
	'messages:apihelp-opensearch-param-redirects-append' => 'en:For historical reasons, the default is "return" for $1format=json and "resolve" for other formats.',
	'messages:apihelp-opensearch-param-warningsaserror' => 'en:If warnings are raised with <kbd>format=json</kbd>, return an API error instead of ignoring them.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-extended-description' => 'en:Only options which are registered in core or in one of installed extensions, or options with keys prefixed with <code>userjs-</code> (intended to be used by user scripts), can be set.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-param-resetkinds' => 'en:List of types of options to reset when the <var>$1reset</var> option is set.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-param-change' => 'en:List of changes, formatted name=value (e.g. skin=vector). If no value is given (not even an equals sign), e.g., optionname|otheroption|..., the option will be reset to its default value. If any value passed contains the pipe character (<kbd>|</kbd>), use the [[Special:ApiHelp/main#main/datatypes|alternative multiple-value separator]] for correct operation.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-param-optionname' => 'en:The name of the option that should be set to the value given by <var>$1optionvalue</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-param-optionvalue' => 'en:The value for the option specified by <var>$1optionname</var>. When <var>$1optionname</var> is set but <var>$1optionvalue</var> is omitted, the option will be reset to its default value.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-param-global' => 'en:What to do if the option was set globally using the GlobalPreferences extension.

* <kbd>ignore</kbd>: Do nothing. The option remains with its previous value.
* <kbd>override</kbd>: Add a local override.
* <kbd>update</kbd>: Update the option globally.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-example-change' => 'en:Change <kbd>skin</kbd> and <kbd>hideminor</kbd> preferences.',
	'messages:apihelp-options-example-complex' => 'en:Reset all preferences, then set <kbd>skin</kbd> and <kbd>nickname</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-summary' => 'en:Obtain information about API modules.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-param-modules' => 'en:List of module names (values of the <var>action</var> and <var>format</var> parameters, or <kbd>main</kbd>). Can specify submodules with a <kbd>+</kbd>, or all submodules with <kbd>+*</kbd>, or all submodules recursively with <kbd>+**</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-param-querymodules' => 'en:List of query module names (value of <var>prop</var>, <var>meta</var> or <var>list</var> parameter). Use <kbd>$1modules=query+foo</kbd> instead of <kbd>$1querymodules=foo</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-param-mainmodule' => 'en:Get information about the main (top-level) module as well. Use <kbd>$1modules=main</kbd> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-param-pagesetmodule' => 'en:Get information about the pageset module (providing titles= and friends) as well.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-param-formatmodules' => 'en:List of format module names (value of <var>format</var> parameter). Use <var>$1modules</var> instead.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-example-1' => 'en:Show info for <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/parse|action=parse]]</kbd>, <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/jsonfm|format=jsonfm]]</kbd>, <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+allpages|action=query&list=allpages]]</kbd>, and <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query+siteinfo|action=query&meta=siteinfo]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-paraminfo-example-2' => 'en:Show info for all submodules of <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query|action=query]]</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-summary' => 'en:Parses content and returns parser output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-extended-description' => 'en:See the various prop-modules of <kbd>[[Special:ApiHelp/query|action=query]]</kbd> to get information from the current version of a page.

There are several ways to specify the text to parse:
# Specify a page or revision, using <var>$1page</var>, <var>$1pageid</var>, or <var>$1oldid</var>.
# Specify content explicitly, using <var>$1text</var>, <var>$1title</var>, <var>$1revid</var>, and <var>$1contentmodel</var>.
# Specify only a summary to parse. <var>$1prop</var> should be given an empty value.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-title' => 'en:Title of page the text belongs to. If omitted, <var>$1contentmodel</var> must be specified, and [[API]] will be used as the title.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-text' => 'en:Text to parse. Use <var>$1title</var> or <var>$1contentmodel</var> to control the content model.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-revid' => 'en:Revision ID, for <code><nowiki>{{REVISIONID}}</nowiki></code> and similar variables.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-summary' => 'en:Summary to parse.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-page' => 'en:Parse the content of this page. Cannot be used together with <var>$1text</var> and <var>$1title</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-pageid' => 'en:Parse the content of this page. Overrides <var>$1page</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-redirects' => 'en:If <var>$1page</var> or <var>$1pageid</var> is set to a redirect, resolve it.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-oldid' => 'en:Parse the content of this revision. Overrides <var>$1page</var> and <var>$1pageid</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-prop' => 'en:Which pieces of information to get:',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-text' => 'en:Gives the parsed text of the wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-langlinks' => 'en:Gives the language links in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-categories' => 'en:Gives the categories in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-categorieshtml' => 'en:Gives the HTML version of the categories.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-templates' => 'en:Gives the templates in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-images' => 'en:Gives the images in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-externallinks' => 'en:Gives the external links in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-sections' => 'en:Gives the sections in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-revid' => 'en:Adds the revision ID of the parsed page.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-headitems' => 'en:Gives items to put in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> of the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-headhtml' => 'en:Gives parsed doctype, opening <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> element and opening <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> of the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-modules' => 'en:Gives the ResourceLoader modules used on the page. To load, use <code>mw.loader.using()</code>. Either <kbd>jsconfigvars</kbd> or <kbd>encodedjsconfigvars</kbd> must be requested jointly with <kbd>modules</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-jsconfigvars' => 'en:Gives the JavaScript configuration variables specific to the page. To apply, use <code>mw.config.set()</code>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-encodedjsconfigvars' => 'en:Gives the JavaScript configuration variables specific to the page as a JSON string.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-indicators' => 'en:Gives the HTML of page status indicators used on the page.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-iwlinks' => 'en:Gives interwiki links in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-wikitext' => 'en:Gives the original wikitext that was parsed.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-properties' => 'en:Gives various properties defined in the parsed wikitext.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-limitreportdata' => 'en:Gives the limit report in a structured way. Gives no data, when <var>$1disablelimitreport</var> is set.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-limitreporthtml' => 'en:Gives the HTML version of the limit report. Gives no data, when <var>$1disablelimitreport</var> is set.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-parsetree' => 'en:The XML parse tree of revision content (requires content model <code>$1</code>)',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-parsewarnings' => 'en:Gives the warnings that occurred while parsing content (as wikitext).',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-paramvalue-prop-parsewarningshtml' => 'en:Gives the warnings that occurred while parsing content (as HTML).',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-wrapoutputclass' => 'en:CSS class to use to wrap the parser output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-usearticle' => 'en:Use the ArticleParserOptions hook to ensure the options used match those used for article page views',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-parsoid' => 'en:Generate HTML conforming to the [[mw:Specs/HTML|MediaWiki DOM spec]] using [[mw:Parsoid|Parsoid]].',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-onlypst' => 'en:Do a pre-save transform (PST) on the input, but don\'t parse it. Returns the same wikitext, after a PST has been applied. Only valid when used with <var>$1text</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-effectivelanglinks' => 'en:Includes language links supplied by extensions (for use with <kbd>$1prop=langlinks</kbd>).',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-section' => 'en:Only parse the content of the section with this identifier.

When <kbd>new</kbd>, parse <var>$1text</var> and <var>$1sectiontitle</var> as if adding a new section to the page.

<kbd>new</kbd> is allowed only when specifying <var>text</var>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-sectiontitle' => 'en:New section title when <var>section</var> is <kbd>new</kbd>.

Unlike page editing, this does not fall back to <var>summary</var> when omitted or empty.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-disablelimitreport' => 'en:Omit the limit report ("NewPP limit report") from the parser output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-disableeditsection' => 'en:Omit edit section links from the parser output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-disablestylededuplication' => 'en:Do not deduplicate inline stylesheets in the parser output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-showstrategykeys' => 'en:Whether to include internal merge strategy information in jsconfigvars.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-generatexml' => 'en:Generate XML parse tree (requires content model <code>$1</code>; replaced by <kbd>$2prop=parsetree</kbd>).',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-sectionpreview' => 'en:Parse in section preview mode (enables preview mode too).',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-disabletoc' => 'en:Omit table of contents in output.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-param-useskin' => 'en:Apply the selected skin to the parser output. May affect the following properties: <kbd>text</kbd>, <kbd>langlinks</kbd>, <kbd>headitems</kbd>, <kbd>modules</kbd>, <kbd>jsconfigvars</kbd>, <kbd>indicators</kbd>.',
	'messages:apihelp-parse-example-texttitle' => 'en:Parse wikitext, specifying the page title.',
